// Does passing a `got` where a `want` is asked for lose information?
//
// ty_rank already orders the numeric types -- width doubled, plus one for
// float -- so this is one comparison rather than a table of pairs: a type
// that outranks the slot it is going into does not fit in it. word into int
// drops 32 bits, float into int drops the fraction, float into word drops it
// too. Everything else widens, which is exact.
ty_narrows(string want, string got) {
  int ok = 0;
  if(ty_num(want) == 1 && ty_num(got) == 1 && ty_rank(want) < ty_rank(got)) {
    ok = 1;
  }
} return int ok;
